Hash speed on AMD EPYC 9255 24-Core Processor (linux7.0.0-38-generic, 48 CPUs), 2026-11-02 22:29:39 UTC
Quick run: 96 rounds; a full run confirms and adds the largest inputs and batches. Each cell is the mean time per unit (total time over total work), lower is better.

In “Batches one after another, buffers owned” and “Batches one after another, buffers lent”, the program hashes one input after another, as fast as it can, alone and with a second program doing the same at once.

SOLO: one copy of each contender, on one thread.

  Batches one after another, buffers owned (ns/msg)
  messages    B3 servil mt
  1024              7.924 

  Batches one after another, buffers lent (ns/msg)
  messages    B3 servil mt
  16                8.199 
  1024              7.063 

SHARED: two copies of the contender at once, each hashing its own input on its own thread, inputs one after another; the time of each copy.

  Batches one after another, buffers owned (ns/msg)
  messages    B3 servil mt
  1024              8.239 

  Batches one after another, buffers lent (ns/msg)
  messages    B3 servil mt
  16                8.166 
  1024              7.042 

